.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BN_CTX_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BN_CTX_new_ex ,
.Nm BN_CTX_new ,
.Nm BN_CTX_secure_new_ex ,
.Nm BN_CTX_secure_new ,
.Nm BN_CTX_free
.Nd allocate and free BN_CTX structures
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/bn.h
.Ft BN_CTX *
.Fo BN_CTX_new_ex
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft BN_CTX *
.Fo BN_CTX_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft BN_CTX *
.Fo BN_CTX_secure_new_ex
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft BN_CTX *
.Fo BN_CTX_secure_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo BN_CTX_free
.Fa "BN_CTX *c"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Vt BN_CTX
is a structure that holds
.Sy BIGNUM
temporary variables used by library functions.
Since dynamic memory allocation to create
.Sy BIGNUM Ns s
is rather expensive when used in conjunction with repeated subroutine
calls, the
.Vt BN_CTX
structure is used.
.Pp
.Fn BN_CTX_new_ex
allocates and initializes a
.Vt BN_CTX
structure for the given library context
.Fa ctx .
The <ctx> value may be NULL in which case the default library context
will be used.
.Fn BN_CTX_new
is the same as
.Fn BN_CTX_new_ex
except that the default library context is always used.
.Pp
.Fn BN_CTX_secure_new_ex
allocates and initializes a
.Vt BN_CTX
structure but uses the secure heap (see
.Xr CRYPTO_secure_malloc 3 )
to hold the
.Sy BIGNUM Ns s
for the given library context
.Fa ctx .
The <ctx> value may be NULL in which case the default library context
will be used.
.Fn BN_CTX_secure_new
is the same as
.Fn BN_CTX_secure_new_ex
except that the default library context is always used.
.Pp
.Fn BN_CTX_free
frees the components of the
.Vt BN_CTX
and the structure itself.
Since
.Xr BN_CTX_start 3
is required in order to obtain
.Sy BIGNUM Ns s
from the
.Vt BN_CTX ,
in most cases
.Xr BN_CTX_end 3
must be called before the
.Vt BN_CTX
may be freed by
.Fn BN_CTX_free .
If
.Fa c
is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
A given
.Vt BN_CTX
must only be used by a single thread of execution.
No locking is performed, and the internal pool allocator will not
properly handle multiple threads of execution.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn BN_CTX_new
and
.Fn BN_CTX_secure_new
return a pointer to the
.Vt BN_CTX .
If the allocation fails, they return
.Dv NULL
and sets an error code that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Pp
.Fn BN_CTX_free
has no return values.
.Sh REMOVED FUNCTIONALITY
.Bd -literal
 void BN_CTX_init(BN_CTX *c);
.Ed
.Xr BN_CTX_init 3
is no longer available as of OpenSSL 1.1.0. Applications should replace
use of BN_CTX_init with BN_CTX_new instead:
.Bd -literal
 BN_CTX *ctx;
 ctx = BN_CTX_new();
 if (!ctx)
     /* error */
 ...
 BN_CTX_free(ctx);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr BN_add 3 ,
.Xr BN_CTX_start 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Xr BN_CTX_init 3
was removed in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
